1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,560
Your scan passes.

2
00:00:01,560 --> 00:00:03,181
The dashboard says Passed.

3
00:00:03,181 --> 00:00:04,304
Everyone is happy.

4
00:00:04,304 --> 00:00:06,175
But what exactly did it check?

5
00:00:06,725 --> 00:00:09,583
And what if your coverage is only fifty-nine percent?

6
00:00:10,133 --> 00:00:14,315
Today we learn the quality gate. The rule that decides, pass or fail.

7
00:00:14,865 --> 00:00:16,170
We build our own gate.

8
00:00:16,170 --> 00:00:18,067
We make a build fail on purpose.

9
00:00:18,067 --> 00:00:19,194
And then we fix it,

10
00:00:19,194 --> 00:00:20,262
and watch it pass.

11
00:00:21,812 --> 00:00:23,241
Here is what to expect.

12
00:00:23,791 --> 00:00:27,439
One: what a quality gate is, and the built-in one, Sonar way.

13
00:00:27,989 --> 00:00:33,088
Two: new code, and overall code. This is the idea that surprises most people.

14
00:00:33,638 --> 00:00:34,881
Three: a live demo.

15
00:00:34,881 --> 00:00:35,992
We copy the gate,

16
00:00:35,992 --> 00:00:37,300
add a coverage rule,

17
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:38,870
attach it to Cloud Cart,

18
00:00:38,870 --> 00:00:39,393
fail it,

19
00:00:39,393 --> 00:00:39,851
fix it,

20
00:00:39,851 --> 00:00:40,635
and pass it.

21
00:00:41,185 --> 00:00:44,983
Four: the limits of a gate, the common mistakes, and the lab files.

22
00:00:45,533 --> 00:00:48,711
This is objective five of the Sonar cube domain.

23
00:00:50,261 --> 00:00:51,584
What is a quality gate?

24
00:00:52,134 --> 00:00:54,602
A gate is a short list of conditions.

25
00:00:54,602 --> 00:00:56,471
Each condition is a measure,

26
00:00:56,471 --> 00:00:57,338
a comparison,

27
00:00:57,338 --> 00:00:58,205
and a number.

28
00:00:58,205 --> 00:00:59,673
For example: coverage,

29
00:00:59,673 --> 00:01:00,541
is less than,

30
00:01:00,541 --> 00:01:01,542
eighty percent.

31
00:01:02,092 --> 00:01:03,208
After every scan,

32
00:01:03,208 --> 00:01:05,374
the server checks each condition.

33
00:01:05,374 --> 00:01:06,490
If one is broken,

34
00:01:06,490 --> 00:01:07,737
the gate is Failed.

35
00:01:07,737 --> 00:01:08,918
If none is broken,

36
00:01:08,918 --> 00:01:09,772
it is Passed.

37
00:01:10,322 --> 00:01:12,328
Sonar way is the built-in gate.

38
00:01:12,328 --> 00:01:13,494
It is the default,

39
00:01:13,494 --> 00:01:15,371
so every new project uses it.

40
00:01:15,371 --> 00:01:17,766
It checks four things: no new issues,

41
00:01:17,766 --> 00:01:19,190
new hotspots reviewed,

42
00:01:19,190 --> 00:01:22,104
coverage on new code at least eighty percent,

43
00:01:22,104 --> 00:01:25,340
and duplication on new code at most three percent.

44
00:01:25,890 --> 00:01:26,962
Notice the word,

45
00:01:26,962 --> 00:01:27,229
new.

46
00:01:27,229 --> 00:01:30,108
Sonar way only judges the code you changed.

47
00:01:30,108 --> 00:01:32,184
It does not judge the old code.

48
00:01:32,734 --> 00:01:35,511
That is a good start for a team with old code.

49
00:01:35,511 --> 00:01:36,718
But it means an old,

50
00:01:36,718 --> 00:01:38,408
weak project can still pass.

51
00:01:39,958 --> 00:01:42,731
So, what is new code, and what is overall code?

52
00:01:43,281 --> 00:01:46,188
New code is what changed since a reference point.

53
00:01:46,188 --> 00:01:48,679
Overall code is everything in the project.

54
00:01:49,229 --> 00:01:52,129
A gate on new code says: do not make it worse.

55
00:01:52,129 --> 00:01:56,290
A gate on overall code says: the whole project must reach a level.

56
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:58,134
Most teams use both.

57
00:01:58,134 --> 00:02:01,045
New code rules keep the quality from falling.

58
00:02:01,045 --> 00:02:02,921
An overall rule sets a floor,

59
00:02:02,921 --> 00:02:04,861
and you raise it step by step.

60
00:02:05,411 --> 00:02:09,763
Two rules. You cannot edit Sonar way. You copy it, and change the copy.

61
00:02:10,313 --> 00:02:14,687
Then you attach the copy to a project. Each project can have its own gate.

62
00:02:16,237 --> 00:02:18,084
Let us start in the browser.

63
00:02:18,084 --> 00:02:20,393
We log in to the Sonar cube server,

64
00:02:20,393 --> 00:02:22,043
with the user name admin,

65
00:02:22,043 --> 00:02:23,428
and the lab password,

66
00:02:23,428 --> 00:02:24,748
which shows as dots.

67
00:02:24,748 --> 00:02:26,331
Then we open Cloud Cart,

68
00:02:26,331 --> 00:02:27,650
on the Summary page.

69
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:40,037
At the top,

70
00:02:40,037 --> 00:02:41,175
the quality gate.

71
00:02:41,175 --> 00:02:41,643
Passed.

72
00:02:41,643 --> 00:02:42,045
Green.

73
00:02:42,045 --> 00:02:45,057
But look at the coverage on the overall code.

74
00:02:45,057 --> 00:02:46,731
About fifty-nine percent.

75
00:02:46,731 --> 00:02:47,400
It passes,

76
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:49,074
and the coverage is weak.

77
00:02:49,074 --> 00:02:49,342
Why?

78
00:02:49,342 --> 00:02:50,948
Let us look at the gate.

79
00:02:51,498 --> 00:02:53,666
We open the Quality Gates page.

80
00:02:53,666 --> 00:02:54,295
One gate,

81
00:02:54,295 --> 00:02:54,995
Sonar way.

82
00:02:54,995 --> 00:02:55,554
Default,

83
00:02:55,554 --> 00:02:56,463
and built in.

84
00:02:56,463 --> 00:02:57,792
You cannot edit it.

85
00:02:58,342 --> 00:02:59,869
Look at the conditions.

86
00:02:59,869 --> 00:03:01,130
They are all under,

87
00:03:01,130 --> 00:03:02,657
Conditions on New Code.

88
00:03:02,657 --> 00:03:03,388
New issues,

89
00:03:03,388 --> 00:03:04,583
hotspots reviewed,

90
00:03:04,583 --> 00:03:05,977
coverage on new code,

91
00:03:05,977 --> 00:03:07,836
and duplication on new code.

92
00:03:07,836 --> 00:03:09,961
Nothing about the whole project.

93
00:03:09,961 --> 00:03:11,952
That is why Cloud Cart passes.

94
00:03:12,502 --> 00:03:17,900
We make our own gate. We click Copy. We give it a name: Cloud Cart gate. And we create it.

95
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:23,608
The copy has the same four conditions.

96
00:03:23,608 --> 00:03:24,658
Now we add one.

97
00:03:24,658 --> 00:03:26,267
We click Add Condition.

98
00:03:26,267 --> 00:03:26,967
We choose,

99
00:03:26,967 --> 00:03:28,086
On Overall Code.

100
00:03:28,086 --> 00:03:29,765
The measure is Coverage.

101
00:03:29,765 --> 00:03:30,885
And the rule is,

102
00:03:30,885 --> 00:03:31,794
is less than,

103
00:03:31,794 --> 00:03:32,494
sixty-two.

104
00:03:32,494 --> 00:03:33,963
We add the condition.

105
00:03:35,613 --> 00:03:37,730
Now the gate has five conditions.

106
00:03:37,730 --> 00:03:42,286
The last one says: overall coverage must be at least sixty-two percent.

107
00:03:42,286 --> 00:03:44,018
Our project has fifty-nine.

108
00:03:44,568 --> 00:03:47,494
A gate does nothing until a project uses it.

109
00:03:47,494 --> 00:03:49,422
We open the project settings,

110
00:03:49,422 --> 00:03:51,151
and the Quality Gate page.

111
00:03:51,151 --> 00:03:51,816
We choose,

112
00:03:51,816 --> 00:03:54,143
Always use a specific quality gate.

113
00:03:54,143 --> 00:03:55,738
We pick Cloud Cart gate.

114
00:03:55,738 --> 00:03:56,337
And save.

115
00:03:56,337 --> 00:04:00,526
Notice the message: the change applies after the next analysis.

116
00:04:01,076 --> 00:04:02,140
Now the terminal.

117
00:04:02,140 --> 00:04:04,205
The gate is checked after a scan,

118
00:04:04,205 --> 00:04:05,269
so we scan again.

119
00:04:05,269 --> 00:04:06,083
Same command,

120
00:04:06,083 --> 00:04:07,710
with the short name: scan.

121
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:11,618
Watch the output.

122
00:04:11,618 --> 00:04:12,488
The tests run,

123
00:04:12,488 --> 00:04:14,416
the coverage report is written,

124
00:04:14,416 --> 00:04:16,468
and the new analysis is uploaded.

125
00:04:16,468 --> 00:04:18,458
The server then checks the gate.

126
00:04:18,458 --> 00:04:20,075
This takes under a minute.

127
00:04:48,325 --> 00:04:49,648
Back in the browser.

128
00:04:49,648 --> 00:04:51,433
We reload the Summary page.

129
00:04:51,433 --> 00:04:52,822
Quality gate: Failed.

130
00:04:52,822 --> 00:04:54,145
And it tells us why.

131
00:04:54,145 --> 00:04:54,740
Coverage,

132
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:55,996
fifty-nine percent,

133
00:04:55,996 --> 00:04:57,518
is less than sixty-two.

134
00:04:57,518 --> 00:04:59,568
That is the condition we added.

135
00:05:00,118 --> 00:05:01,063
In a pipeline,

136
00:05:01,063 --> 00:05:02,954
this Failed stops the build.

137
00:05:02,954 --> 00:05:05,251
Let us prove it from the terminal.

138
00:05:05,251 --> 00:05:05,926
Lab check.

139
00:05:05,926 --> 00:05:07,209
The token is valid.

140
00:05:07,209 --> 00:05:09,235
The project uses its own gate.

141
00:05:09,235 --> 00:05:11,194
The gate has a coverage rule.

142
00:05:11,194 --> 00:05:13,017
But the gate is not Passed.

143
00:05:13,017 --> 00:05:13,963
Three of four.

144
00:05:14,513 --> 00:05:15,389
Now we fix it.

145
00:05:15,389 --> 00:05:17,079
We do not lower the number.

146
00:05:17,079 --> 00:05:17,892
We add tests.

147
00:05:17,892 --> 00:05:20,583
We write a test class for the pricing code,

148
00:05:20,583 --> 00:05:22,711
the file with the lowest coverage.

149
00:05:22,711 --> 00:05:23,837
Seven small tests,

150
00:05:23,837 --> 00:05:25,339
each one calls a method,

151
00:05:25,339 --> 00:05:26,716
and checks the result.

152
00:05:27,266 --> 00:05:29,719
We check the file is there. And we scan again.

153
00:05:34,369 --> 00:05:34,758
Again,

154
00:05:34,758 --> 00:05:35,667
the tests run.

155
00:05:35,667 --> 00:05:36,964
Now there are forty,

156
00:05:36,964 --> 00:05:38,327
and all of them pass.

157
00:05:38,327 --> 00:05:40,338
The coverage report is written,

158
00:05:40,338 --> 00:05:42,220
and the analysis is uploaded.

159
00:06:16,270 --> 00:06:17,559
Back in the browser.

160
00:06:17,559 --> 00:06:19,300
We reload the Summary page.

161
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:20,654
Quality gate: Passed.

162
00:06:20,654 --> 00:06:21,234
Coverage,

163
00:06:21,234 --> 00:06:22,459
sixty-four percent.

164
00:06:22,459 --> 00:06:23,877
It is above sixty-two.

165
00:06:23,877 --> 00:06:24,973
The number moved,

166
00:06:24,973 --> 00:06:26,779
because we added real tests,

167
00:06:26,779 --> 00:06:27,939
and scanned again.

168
00:06:28,489 --> 00:06:33,737
Finally, the proof. Lab check. Four of four. Own gate, coverage rule, and Passed.

169
00:06:36,287 --> 00:06:39,338
The results are saved in a file. That is your evidence.

170
00:06:40,888 --> 00:06:42,381
Now, the limits of a gate.

171
00:06:42,931 --> 00:06:48,137
A gate is only as good as its rules. If the rules are weak, the gate passes weak code.

172
00:06:48,687 --> 00:06:49,975
A gate can be gamed.

173
00:06:49,975 --> 00:06:51,844
Someone can lower the number,

174
00:06:51,844 --> 00:06:53,841
or exclude files from the scan,

175
00:06:53,841 --> 00:06:54,937
to turn it green.

176
00:06:54,937 --> 00:06:58,159
A pass that you did not earn is worse than a fail.

177
00:06:58,709 --> 00:07:00,627
And a gate cannot see everything.

178
00:07:00,627 --> 00:07:02,895
It does not know if the design is good,

179
00:07:02,895 --> 00:07:04,697
or if the tests check anything.

180
00:07:04,697 --> 00:07:06,965
It only checks the numbers you gave it.

181
00:07:07,515 --> 00:07:10,693
So: few rules, clear rules, and raise them slowly.

182
00:07:12,243 --> 00:07:13,395
Five mistakes.

183
00:07:13,945 --> 00:07:18,382
One: editing the numbers, to make a failed gate pass. Fix the code instead.

184
00:07:18,932 --> 00:07:21,994
Two: forgetting to attach the gate to the project.

185
00:07:21,994 --> 00:07:23,524
The default gate is used,

186
00:07:23,524 --> 00:07:25,055
and your rule never runs.

187
00:07:25,605 --> 00:07:30,085
Three: forty rules. Nobody understands why the build failed. Keep a few.

188
00:07:30,635 --> 00:07:36,075
Four: a rule on new code only, for a project with old weak code. It never improves.

189
00:07:36,625 --> 00:07:38,374
Five: reading the dashboard,

190
00:07:38,374 --> 00:07:39,998
but not failing the build.

191
00:07:39,998 --> 00:07:40,747
Next lesson,

192
00:07:40,747 --> 00:07:42,684
we connect the gate to Jenkins.

193
00:07:44,234 --> 00:07:47,029
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

194
00:07:47,579 --> 00:07:49,043
One: the repository,

195
00:07:49,043 --> 00:07:53,363
git hub dot com slash it dash waves slash dev ops dash A I,

196
00:07:53,363 --> 00:07:55,707
in the folder academy slash lab.

197
00:07:56,257 --> 00:08:02,187
Two: the files, lab one sixty-eight dot S H, and shortcuts one sixty-eight dot S H.

198
00:08:02,737 --> 00:08:04,679
Three: load the short names,

199
00:08:04,679 --> 00:08:07,868
with source shortcuts one sixty-eight dot S H.

200
00:08:07,868 --> 00:08:11,127
Then scan runs the Maven command with Ja Co Co,

201
00:08:11,127 --> 00:08:13,276
and lab check tests the result.

202
00:08:13,826 --> 00:08:16,239
Four: set the variable Sonar token,

203
00:08:16,239 --> 00:08:17,825
to your own user token.

204
00:08:17,825 --> 00:08:20,653
Never put it in a file in the repository.

205
00:08:21,203 --> 00:08:22,507
Five: copy the gate,

206
00:08:22,507 --> 00:08:23,941
add the coverage rule,

207
00:08:23,941 --> 00:08:24,593
attach it,

208
00:08:24,593 --> 00:08:25,180
and scan.

209
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:26,028
Make it fail.

210
00:08:26,028 --> 00:08:27,006
Then add tests,

211
00:08:27,006 --> 00:08:28,115
and make it pass.

212
00:08:28,665 --> 00:08:30,307
The link is in the description.

213
00:08:31,857 --> 00:08:32,732
Your turn.

214
00:08:33,282 --> 00:08:37,442
One: open Quality Gates, and read the four conditions of Sonar way.

215
00:08:37,992 --> 00:08:42,877
Two: copy it, and add a coverage rule on overall code, a little above your number.

216
00:08:43,427 --> 00:08:47,118
Three: attach the gate to your project, and scan. Does it fail?

217
00:08:47,668 --> 00:08:50,548
Four: add tests, and scan again, until it passes.

218
00:08:51,098 --> 00:08:53,743
Five: run lab check, and get four of four.

219
00:08:54,293 --> 00:08:56,021
Pause the video, and do it now.

220
00:09:11,571 --> 00:09:12,446
Quick check.

221
00:09:12,996 --> 00:09:14,318
What is a quality gate?

222
00:09:14,868 --> 00:09:17,450
Why can an old weak project pass Sonar way?

223
00:09:17,999 --> 00:09:20,602
Why do you copy Sonar way, and not edit it?

224
00:09:21,152 --> 00:09:23,286
What is the wrong way to make a gate pass?

225
00:09:23,836 --> 00:09:29,254
Objective covered: M C eighteen, objective five. The quality gate and its limits.

226
00:09:29,804 --> 00:09:31,874
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

